verdicts.recommended_fix:
Add a deterministic cleanup step to the R7 build, either after the shift in r7_pcb.py or in r7_post.py. A hand edit would be lost, because r7_build.sh restores R6 from git and rebuilds.

1. Delete every untouched-R6 track whose copper is wholly covered by other copper of the same net and layer (tracks, pads and vias). In my scratch test that was 105 tracks; it left 0 clearance violations and 0 unconnected items.
2. Re-terminate the 8 ends this exposes, and remove the hidden fold-back stubs:
   - shorten the RAW_ACT_SENSE In2 0.2 mm trunk to end at (14.63, 73.0);
   - VBUS In2 at (12.6, 80.55);
   - 3V3 B.Cu at (24.9, 34.2);
   - VLOGIC F.Cu at (27.57, 27.2), and the two VLOGIC B.Cu tracks into via (26.905, 29.45);
   - PYRO1_GATE at (25.377, 91.775);
   - the 25 µm USB_LIMITED stub at (28.725, 57.0).
3. Redraw the roughly 40 remaining sites (partial side-by-side overlaps and same-net crossings) as a single 0°/45°/90° centreline inside the existing copper of that net. Use the width already there, or the wider one where the net carries current; IPC-2152 sizing happens to hold for 0.4 mm on USB_LIMITED. Do this together with the RG-07 and RG-08 fixes, since the same sites carry the micro-segments and jogs.
4. Rerun the overlap scan until all overlap categories are zero, then run DRC, check_r7 and check_actuators. Re-baseline check_actuators wherever SERVO3_OUT, PYRO1_GATE, PYRO1_OUT, PYRO1_CONT_MCU, ARM1_SENSE or ACT_GATE copper changes.

Restate the finding as 93 separate sites (about 185 overlapping pairs) rather than 247 instances.

Do not redraw each hook one by one.
1. PYRO1_COLD: delete the dead branch:
   - F.Cu (28.72,85.1)→(28.72,84.5) and the tail of R131's trace beyond the D120 junction;
   - vias (28.72,84.5), (25.25,90.3) and (18.85,102.7);
   - the B.Cu/In2 chain out to (18.95,112.3), including the 3 micro-segments.
   Then rejoin R131.2→D120.1 at 0.2 mm width: (29.72,86.1)→(29.72,85.33)→(31.05,84.0).
2. IMU_CS: delete the In2 branch:
   - vias (25.1,66.77) and (30.8,66.77) and the In2 segment between them;
   - F.Cu (31.4,66.77)→(38.5,73.87)→(38.5,76.97)→(37.2,78.27)→(37.2,80.07);
   - the jogs at (24.35–25.1,66.75–66.77).
   End the direct diagonal at (37.2,79.6), then run a vertical to the via (37.2,80.07).
3. SPI1_MOSI: replace the route with one 45° diagonal (23.35,66.30)→(34.6,77.55), then a vertical to the via (34.6,80.96). The vertical from U1.91 now ends at y 66.30. MOSI then runs parallel to IMU_CS at 0.189 mm, and C121.1 stays at 0.194 mm.
   Steps 1–3 together were checked on a scratch copy: DRC with zone refill found 0 violations and 0 unconnected.
4. Clear the remaining hooks and micro-segments with a script:
   - snap segment ends to the via or pad centre;
   - delete segments under 50 µm whose ends both lie in same-net copper;
   - merge collinear segments.
   Afterwards rerun a dead-copper and loop scan, not just KiCad's dangling check, because micro-loops hide open ends from it. The same scan also flags loops on USB_LIMITED (101 mm), 3V3A, CAM_IO_3V3, 3V3 and RAW_PROTECTED for the overlap findings. Then rerun the gate.
5. Remove PYRO1_CONT (blocked by SWDIO and R77.1) and SPI1_SCK's main offset from the fix list.
